From 7f921fb4119d622d70caef3871a5229e298267b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:53:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0115 -- report build_dirty in the run
 manifest

binary_sha12 alone cannot say whether a cell ran a binary built from
uncommitted source. Since the Makefile now folds the vendor trees' dirty
state into that stamp, two such builds do at least get different hashes --
but a reader seeing two different hex strings learns only that they
differ, not that either was built from a working tree. This says so
outright.

The need is not hypothetical. Three benchmark binaries in one day were
stamped with a tree they were not built from: an A/B arm built by
reverse-applying a patch to the working tree, a B arm built before its own
commit, and a confirmation cell carrying the previous patch's identity and
colliding with a live ABBA arm. Every one failed silently, and in the
direction that PASSES the "the two arms must differ" invalidity check.

Emitted as its own line rather than as a "-dirty" suffix on binary_sha12,
because that field is fixed-width in the manifest struct. Absent the
compile flag it reports -1 (unknown) rather than 0, so a build stage that
omits the flag cannot be misread as a clean build.
---
 Engine/main/quit.cpp | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/main/quit.cpp b/Engine/main/quit.cpp
index 79ab5d20b..53301f9e5 100644
--- a/Engine/main/quit.cpp
+++ b/Engine/main/quit.cpp
@@ -575,6 +575,28 @@ void quit(const char *quitmsg)
                 }
             }
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+            // patch 0115: was this a WORKING-TREE build?
+            //
+            // binary_sha12 alone cannot say. It is derived from the
+            // committed vendor trees plus (since this patch) their dirty
+            // state, so two builds differing only in uncommitted edits now
+            // get different stamps -- but a reader seeing two different
+            // hex strings learns that they differ, not that either one was
+            // built from uncommitted source. This line says so outright.
+            //
+            // Deliberately its own line rather than a "-dirty" suffix on
+            // binary_sha12: that field is fixed-width in the manifest
+            // struct.
+            fprintf(run_manifest_log, "DOS-PORT build_dirty=%d\n",
+#ifdef PORT_BUILD_DIRTY
+                    (int)(PORT_BUILD_DIRTY)
+#else
+                    -1  // flag absent: unknown, not "clean"
+#endif
+                    );
+#endif
+
 #ifdef __DJGPP__
             // patch 0114: did this run EVER need color_map?
             {
